course: dictionary
lesson: 759
title: The verb be
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Be is a small word, but it is one of the most used in English. Its forms are am, is, are, was, were, been and being. Use am with I, is with he, she and it, and are with you, we and they. «Some children are adopted» uses are because children means more than one.
explain: Be tells you what something is like or where it is. «Chloe and Bella are still frenemies» tells you what they are. «A blurry or faraway photo is not real proof» tells you what kind of photo it is. Be also helps other verbs, as in «I am running».
explain: Be can also say that something exists. «There is at least one day a year when the Sun does not set» means that such a day exists. In maths, is often means equals: 3 + 4 is 7.
fact: Be is a verb, and its form changes with the subject: I am, he is, they are.
fact: Was and were are the past forms: «It was cloudy» and «You were right».
fact: Be can help other verbs: «The cake was eaten» and «I am running».
fact: Short forms join be to another word: I'm, he's, they're, isn't, aren't, wasn't and weren't.
exercise: Which form of be goes in the gap? «Ben ___ seven years old.» | was | *is | are | be
exercise: In «3 + 4 is 7», what does is mean? | Lives in | Shouts | *Equals | Is a kind of food
exercise: Which short form means «is not»? | aren't | wasn't | *isn't | weren't
test: Which form of be goes with I? | be | are | *am | is
test: What is the past form of is? | being | be | are | *was
exam: Which sentence uses a form of be in the passive voice, like «It is given that»? | *The test is marked by the teacher. | She ran home. | The teacher marks the test. | Dogs bark loudly.
